  "507": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "[VISUAL]: A cinematic handheld medium close-up vlog shot of the same young woman from the reference image, preserving her exact facial features, almond-shaped hazel eyes, fair warm skin, long straight dark brown hair, elegant jawline, and natural beauty. She is dressed as a noblewoman in medieval Spain (late 13th century), wearing an intricately embroidered olive-green silk gown with gold trim and subtle medieval jewelry. She holds the camera at arm's length as if filming a modern travel vlog while walking through the bustling streets of medieval Toledo. Behind her are narrow cobblestone alleys, sandstone buildings, wooden balconies draped with colorful fabrics, market stalls selling bread, pottery, spices, and woven textiles, blacksmiths working, horses, townsfolk in authentic medieval clothing, monks, merchants, and castle guards moving naturally in the background. Warm golden afternoon sunlight creates beautiful volumetric rays and soft cinematic rim lighting on her hair. The camera exhibits realistic handheld micro-movements, natural walking bounce, subtle autofocus breathing, slight exposure adaptation, and shallow depth of field while maintaining continuous eye contact. The woman occasionally smiles, gestures toward the market behind her, and looks around with genuine curiosity while continuing to address the audience. Ultra-photorealistic, historically accurate medieval Spain, 35mm cinema lens, f/2.0, HDR, natural colors, high dynamic range, soft film grain, documentary realism, immersive cinematic atmosphere.\n\n[SPEECH]: Welcome, everyone! Today I'm taking you with me through the streets of medieval Spain. Behind me is one of the busiest marketplaces in Toledo, where merchants from across Europe, North Africa, and the Mediterranean come to trade spices, fabrics, and handcrafted goods. The streets are crowded, the air smells of fresh bread and wood smoke, and every corner has a story to tell. Let's explore what daily life was really like more than seven hundred years ago.\n\n[SOUNDS]: Natural outdoor medieval ambience with lively market chatter in the distance, footsteps on cobblestone streets, horses trotting past, wagon wheels creaking, blacksmith hammering metal, merchants calling to customers, birds overhead, light wind, church bells ringing occasionally, fabric fluttering from balconies. The speaker has a warm, engaging, conversational vlog tone, speaking close to the microphone with clean, clear voice capture. Soft medieval instrumental background music featuring lute, vihuela, recorder, and gentle frame drum plays quietly beneath the dialogue without overpowering the narration."
    },
